<body>
    <h1>Consul Installation &amp; Configuration</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-Prerequisites"><stro=
ng>Prerequisites</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Consul installed via vanilla installation.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Access to servers running Consul.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Let=E2=80=99s Encrypt certificates configured for your domain (e.g., <co=
de>lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com</code>).</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-Step1:VanillaInstallation"><=
strong>Step 1: Vanilla Installation</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-1.ConsulSetupDirectory">1. <=
strong>Consul Setup Directory</strong></h3>
<p>Create a universal path for Consul files:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">CONSUL_=
BASE=3D"${HOME}/consul"=20
mkdir -p "${CONSUL_BASE}/setup" "${CONSUL_BASE}/data/{checks,services}" "${=
CONSUL_BASE}/certs"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-2.DownloadBinaries">2. <stro=
ng>Download Binaries</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">cd "${C=
ONSUL_BASE}/setup"
wget https://releases.hashicorp.com/consul/1.21.1/consul_1.21.1_linux_amd64=
.zip
unzip consul_1.21.1_linux_amd64.zip
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-3.MoveConsulto~/bin"><strong=
>3. Move Consul to </strong><code>~/bin</code><strong> </strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">mkdir -=
p ~/bin        =20
mv consul ~/bin/     =20
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-4.Add~/bintoYourPATH"><stron=
g>4. Add </strong><code>~/bin</code><strong> to Your </strong><code>PATH</c=
ode></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">echo 'e=
xport PATH=3D"$HOME/bin:$PATH"' &gt;&gt; ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc     =20
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-5.VerifyInstallation"><stron=
g>5. Verify Installation</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">consul =
--version</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>(Should output: </em><code>Consul v1.21.1</code><em>)</em></p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-Step2:TLSConfiguration"><str=
ong>Step 2: TLS Configuration</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-1.SymlinkingLet'sEncryptCert=
ificatesforConsul">1. Symlinking Let's Encrypt Certificates for Consul</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">ln -sf =
/etc/letsencrypt/live/yourdomain.com/fullchain.pem "${CONSUL_BASE}/certs/"
ln -sf /etc/letsencrypt/live/yourdomain.com/privkey.pem "${CONSUL_BASE}/cer=
ts/"
ln -sf /etc/letsencrypt/live/yourdomain.com/chain.pem "${CONSUL_BASE}/certs=
/"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-2.CreateConfigFile(${CONSUL_=
BASE}/consul-secure.hcl)">2. Create Config File (<code>${CONSUL_BASE}/consu=
l-secure.hcl</code>)</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">datacen=
ter =3D "dc1"
data_dir =3D "${CONSUL_BASE}/data"
server =3D true
bootstrap_expect =3D 1
node_name =3D "lambda1-dev"

# Network
bind_addr =3D "YOUR_SERVER_IP" =20
advertise_addr =3D "YOUR_SERVER_IP"
client_addr =3D "0.0.0.0"=20
# TLS

tls {
  defaults {
    cert_file =3D "${CONSUL_BASE}/certs/fullchain.pem"
    key_file =3D "${CONSUL_BASE}/certs/privkey.pem"
    ca_file =3D "${CONSUL_BASE}/certs/chain.pem"
    verify_incoming =3D true
    verify_outgoing =3D true
  }
  https {
    verify_incoming =3D false
  }
  grpc {
    use_auto_cert =3D false
  }
}

# UI
ui_config {
  enabled =3D true
}

# Ports
ports {
  https =3D 8500
  http =3D -1
  grpc =3D -1
  grpc_tls =3D 8503
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"ConsulInstallation&amp;Configuration-Step3:StartConsul"><strong>S=
tep 3: Start Consul</strong></h2>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">~/bin/c=
onsul agent -dev -config-file=3D"${CONSUL_BASE}/consul-secure.hcl"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Once the agent is running, you can access the Consul Web UI securely via=
 HTTPS:</p>
<p><strong>UI URL:</strong> <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://10.1=
61.244.15:8500/ui" rel=3D"nofollow">https://10.161.244.15:8500/ui</a> (for =
the <code>lambda1</code> server)</p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
